      <workList xml:id="workDesc_41f8217d">
         <work xml:id="work_95N2004F">
            <identifier label="SchW" xml:id="identifier_aae253ca">A2:003</identifier>
            <title xml:id="title_2f92c152" xml:lang="en">Sinfonia</title>
            <title type="alternative" xml:id="title_495663cd" xml:lang="en">Concerto for violin</title>
            <contributor xml:id="respStmt_a7001f77">
               <persName role="composer" xml:id="persName_d391fb3e">Johann Adolph Scheibe</persName>
            </contributor>
            <creation xml:id="creation_f4327bcf">
               <date isodate="1750" xml:id="date_e3d46e8f">before 1750</date>
            </creation>
            <history xml:id="history_e75164ee">
               <p xml:id="idm68">The present work, which might either be a sinfonia in F major or a violin concerto in F major, has not survived. It is listed in the catalogue the Fürstlich zu Bentheim-Tecklenburgische Musikbibliothek with a two-bar incipit. <persName xml:id="idm69" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Count Moritz Casimir I</persName>, who reigned 1710–68, played both the flute and cello in the daily court concerts which took place each evening before dinner ('Tafel'). Since the catalogue was begun in 1750, the work must have been part of the music collection before that date and hence might be one of the works which Scheibe mentions in his autobiography of 1739 (Mattheson's <rend xml:id="idm70" fontstyle="italic">Grundlage, </rend>1740; SchW C5:001).</p>
            </history>
